- Python 3.x
- tkinter (stdlib - native Windows GUI)
- ctypes (Windows API: user32.dll, winmm.dll, kernel32.dll, SetWindowLong for click-through) — Windows only
- threading (async listener + keyboard hook)
- queue.Queue (action dispatch from hook threads to main thread)
- json (profile storage)
- os (file path)
- time (delays, key state timestamps)
- atexit (cleanup)
- struct (Linux: evdev input_event parsing)
- subprocess (Linux: ydotool for input sim)
- glob — Linux evdev device discovery

Architecture:
  engine/_plat_win32.py — Windows backend (ctypes, WH_MOUSE_LL, SendInput)
  engine/_plat_linux.py — Linux backend  (ydotool + evdev)
  engine/input_sim.py, hook.py, shortcuts.py — sys.platform dispatchers
  engine/macros.py — platform-agnostic (uses click_left/right, press_key)
  app/             — tkinter UI (imports engine, never reverse)
